Name: dav_writelock_max_timeout
Type: DURATION
Default-Value: 5m
Last-Modified: UNRELEASED

The longest lifetime granted to a WebDAV write lock (RFC 4918).  A LOCK
request may ask for a lifetime in its Timeout header, either as
"Second-N" or "Infinite"; the server grants the first one it understands,
capped at this value.  A request without a usable Timeout gets five
minutes, also capped.  The default keeps the historical behaviour, where
every lock lasted five minutes whatever the client asked for.
